<title>JAPAN: MOF says to hold 2-yr note auction on Thursday.</title>
<headline>MOF says to hold 2-yr note auction on Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finance Ministry is planning to offer two-year Japanese government notes through a price competitive auction on Thursday, a ministry official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>MOF offered 120 bln yen worth of 0.7 percent two-year notes at its previous two-year note auction in March.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
</text>
